NARRATOR: Arun is packing his bag when his phone rings. "Nithish amma". His hands start to shake.
  ta: Arun bag pack pannitu irukumbodhu phone adikkudhu. "Nithish amma". Kai nadunga aarambikkudhu.
@pose arun phone
@shot on arun
AMMA: Arun, can you hear me, pa? Where's Nithish? I called him four or five times; it just says switched off.
  ta: Arun, kekudha-pa? Nithish angaya pa irukan? Avan-uku naan naal-anju vaati adichan. Aana 'chuch-aap' nu vandhuchu.
ARUN: His phone must have run out of charge, amma. Don't worry. He's gone out with friends, on some project work. He'll be back.
  ta: Phone-la charge theendhu poirukum-ma, neenga onnum bayap-padadheenga. Avan yedho project velaiya poran-nu sonnan ma. Avan vandhuruvan.
AMMA: Ask him to call me as soon as he comes. Don't forget, pa. Look after yourself.
  ta: Sari avan vandha odaney yenakku adikka solriya? Marakkama koopda sollu-pa. Odamba pathuko.
ARUN: Yes, amma. I'll tell him.
  ta: Sari ma, kandippa solren.
@pose arun think
@shot close arun
NARRATOR: The lie sits heavy on him. Arun holds his head in both hands.
  ta: Andha poi avan mela baarama irukku. Arun rendu kaiyaalum thalaiya pudichukkuraan.
